  "summary": "Hand-cut glazed terracotta tile mosaic forming infinite geometric star patterns across Moroccan and Andalusi surfaces.",
  "description": "Maâlems (master craftsmen) hand-chisel glazed tiles (enamel-fired Fès clay) into tesserae assembled face-down into girih-derived star polygons — eight-point khatim, sixteen-fold rosettes — cladding fountains, riads, mosques and minarets. The mathematical discipline (related to Penrose-adjacent quasi-periodic patterns documented by physicists) expresses infinity without figuration. Zellige thrives in Fès and Marrakech workshops and in global Moroccan-revival design.",
